     if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            truncated = _truncate_message(message, self.max_message_chars)\n            if truncated != message:\n                saved = (record.msg, record.args, record.__dict__.pop(\"message\", None))\n                record.msg = truncated\n                record.args = ()\n        try:\n            msg = super().format(record)\n        finally:\n            if saved is not None:\n                record.msg, record.args = saved[0], saved[1]\n                if saved[2] is not None:\n                    record.__dict__[\"message\"] = saved[2]\n```\n\nHmm, popping \"message\" and restoring only if not None — if it wasn't present, pop returns None and we don't restore; fine. But careful: super().format sets record.message to truncated text; we must remove it or restore. Restoring original if existed; else delete. Let me write:\n\n```python\n        finally:\n            if saved is not None:\n                record.msg, record.args, cached_message = saved\n                if cached_message is _MISSING:\n                    record.__dict__.pop(\"message\", None)\n                else:\n                    record.__dict__[\"message\"] = cached_message\n```\n\nUse a sentinel. Define `_MISSING = object()` module-level.\n\nNote: `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True` — good; `1 is not True` → True so truncated, correct requirement (only exact True keeps full).\n\nTruncation helper:\n\n```python\n_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\n\ndef _truncate_message(message: str, max_chars: int) -> str:\n    if len(message) <= max_chars:\n        return message\n    marker = _TRUNCATION_MARKER\n    remaining = max_chars - len(marker)\n    if remaining <= 0:\n        return marker[:max_chars]  # hmm\n```\n\nWith max>=32 and marker length 15, remaining >=17. Head = ceil(remaining/2), tail = remaining - head. e