es error. Let's think about the compat tests: they load the module fresh (importlib) maybe with env var set to 64 and check the default handler's formatter truncates. Reading at import is right.\n\nAlternatively read inside _setup_logger but with a defensive lazy read... keep simple.\n\nActually there's a subtlety: formatter creation happens on every _setup_logger call (even when handler exists), so re-init applies cached config. Good.\n\nNow stats_logger: in `_log_worker`, change `logger.info(m)` to `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nLet me also check logger.py end to see full file (init_logger, _print_error_line etc.) — I read lines 1-110 partially. I should read the rest to avoid breaking things, and I need to make precise replacements. Let me read lines 110-end.\n\nAlso need to check whether envs is imported in logger.py currently — no. Need import: `from deepinfer import envs`. Check for circular imports: environ.py imports only os, threading, collections.abc, datetime, typing. So safe.\n\nLet me read rest of logger.py."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 10124, "completion_tokens": 1598, "total_tokens": 11722, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4096}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 1549}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4096, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 6028}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
